# Project context

- Game: Steel Conveyor War — Factorio-like 2D PvP factory/RTS MVP prototype on .NET 10 + SFML.
- Integration branch: `develop`. Release branch: `main`.
- Sources of truth in order: `docs/MVP_IMPLEMENTATION_DECISIONS.md`, `docs/MVP_GDD.md`, `docs/ТЗ.md`, `docs/agents/`.
- Core stays headless and deterministic. SFML only adapts window/input/render.
- Runtime loads `config/game.json`, `research.json`, `tiles.json`, `entities.json`, `build-costs.json` (Core parse; `SteelConveyorWar.Hosting` I/O for Client/Headless). Recipes/combat/footprints/stacks/power still live in `MvpDefinitions.cs` — do not pretend those domains are data-driven yet.
- Keep catalog ids and C# constants in sync with current names (`.cursor/rules/research-ids.mdc`).
- `SteelConveyorWar.Headless` is the Core+Hosting host for bots/CI (no SFML window). Client remains the SFML composition root.
- Never merge, approve PRs, or force-push protected branches. Hand off merge-ready PRs to a human.
- Prefer `eng/verify.ps1` after meaningful changes. Core tests must not reference SFML.
